 why didn't you speak and I said  because you ain't answer question and  Whoopi and she said speak up or be left  behind  and that's when I learned now you can't  get me to shut up  um but I learned to speak up you know  sometimes you can't follow the rules you  got to take risks you got to be fearless  and that's what I learned from Barbara  be curious be Fearless don't take no for  an answer and when it came to life off  camera the ladies had a close Bond and  Barbara she wasn't afraid to talk Hot  Topics at home what you saw on the show  versus one-on-one with Barbara  completely different whenever like I  said on The View whenever Barb would say  I want to have dinner with you dude I  want to have dinner with you dear I was  like what did I do now we would go out  to dinner hold hands laugh so much we  talked about sex non-stop she gave me  marriage advice literally Barbara said  you always get with men who take your  money don't get married anymore you need  to become a lesbian but nothing she said  come to think of it a lesbian would  probably take your money too so I mean  that was like Barbara she had a  wonderful Wicked it sense of humor and  she supported me in everything I did  came to every show that I did she just  was supportive and loving and funny you  know if you're doing something and  Barbara saw it you always got a  handwritten note that's one thing that I  learned from Barbara I got a thousand  cars that say Sherry that you know  handwritten notes are really important  so it wasn't that she would call it was  that you would get a note in the mail  saying I support you you were lovely  darling I have those notes you know  still that Barbara sent me as for  Barbara's Legacy Sherry says she's left  a long lasting impact you know every  show that has a panel is an offshoot of  The View when you hear talk shows with  the and the and the noun behind it or  the adjective The Chew the real the talk  every ESPN panel that is an offshoot of  Barbara show 